# Every change to the default branch needs an approving review from the repository
# owner. Combined with `require_code_owner_review` in the `Main branch` ruleset, this
# is what keeps the loop from merging its own work: the loop may open a pull request
# against any path — including `scripts/loop/**`, the host it runs on — but it cannot
# approve it (GitHub forbids approving your own PR) and a bot approval never
# satisfies this rule, so a human has to say yes.
#
# Pull requests are evaluated against the CODEOWNERS of their *base* branch, so a PR
# cannot rewrite the ownership it is subject to. The GitHub docs also recommend
# owning this file and the directory it lives in explicitly, which is why they are
# listed below: a silent edit to them would otherwise be a way to shed review.
#
# Note for dependabot PRs: they are covered by `*` too, so they need the owner's
# approval before merging (the owner's ruleset bypass still allows merging them
# without a second reviewer).

*                       @Alex1990
/.github/               @Alex1990
/scripts/               @Alex1990
